[tool_result]Web search results for query: "Li2MnO3 oxygen redox 4.5 V plateau activation voltage lithium-rich layered oxide"  Links: [{"title":"The layered Li- rich oxides also display an activation \"plateau\" (absent for layered oxides) at around 4.5 V after the active tr...","url":"https://www.fleckmech.org/papers/379.pdf#16#3"},{"title":"Unravelling the Chemical and Structural Evolution of Mn and Ti in Disordered Rocksalt Oxyfluoride Cathode Materials Using Operando X-ray Absorption Spectroscopy - - 35Strehle, B","url":"https://pubs-acs-org-443.webvpna.lzu.edu.cn/doi/full/10.1021/acs.chemmater.3c01446#13"},{"title":"Influence of Calendering on the Electrochemical Performance of LiNi0.9Mn0.05Al0.05O2 Cathodes in Lithium-Ion Cells - - 39Strehle, B","url":"https://pubs-acs-org-443.webvpna.lzu.edu.cn/doi/full/10.1021/acsami.1c12543#8"},{"title":"The double-edged oxygen: Harnessing anionic redox in lithium-rich manganese-based cathode materials - Fig","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2950264026000687#2"},{"title":"상세정보 - 상세정보","url":"https://library.cnu.ac.kr/eds/detail/edsker_edsker.000005143478?briefLink=%2Feds%2Fbrief%2FdiscoveryResult%3Fq%3D%2522%25EC%25B0%25A8%25EC%2584%25B8%25EB%258C%2580%2B%25EC%2596%2591%25EA%25B7%25B9%25EC%259E%25AC%2522%26service_type%3Dbrief%26si%3DSU%26st%3DKWRD%26#1"},{"title":"Co-Free Layered Cathode Materials for High Energy Density Lithium-Ion Batteries - Owing to the limited performance of Li2MnO3, various alternatives have been proposed to enhance its properties, thereby leading ...","url":"https://pubs-acs-org-443.webvpna.lzu.edu.cn/doi/10.1021/acsenergylett.0c00742#2"},{"title":"Effect of the Cooling Process on the Structure and Charge/Discharge Cycling Performance in Li[Li0.20Mn0.58Ni0.18Co0.04]O2 Li-rich Solid-Solution Layered Oxide Cathode Materials for Li-Ion Battery","url":"https://ecs.confex.com/ecs/233/webprogram/Paper107192.html"},{"title":"Structural and Chemical Evolution of the Layered Li-Excess LixMnO3 as a Function of Li Content from First-Principles Calculations - Structural and Chemical Evolution of the Layered Li-Excess LixMnO3 as a Function of Li Content from First-Principles Calculation...","url":"https://www.osti.gov/biblio/1511383#1"},{"title":"OUCI - 16 публікацій · Експортувати","url":"https://ouci.dntb.gov.ua/?backlinks_to=10.1007%2Fs12274-014-0563-3&sort=title-asc#1"},{"title":"Layered-to-Spinel Phase Transformation of Li2MnO3 during the Initial Charge - The following article is Free article","url":"https://beta.iopscience.iop.org/article/10.1149/MA2017-02/2/129#1"}]  The ~4.5 V plateau in Li-rich layered oxides is the **initial-charge activation plateau of the Li2MnO3 component**. Li-rich/LMR cathodes are often described as \(x\text{Li}_2\text{MnO}_3\cdot(1-x)\text{LiMO}_2\) and contain Li2MnO3- and LiMO2-rich nanodomains; this plateau is absent in conventional layered oxides. Li2MnO3 is initially electrochemically inactive but becomes active when charged above ~4.5 V vs Li/Li⁺; after activation, Li-rich cathodes can deliver capacities over 250 mAh g⁻¹.  **Oxygen redox mechanism** - First-principles work on Li\(_x\)MnO\(_3\) (\(0 \le x \le 2\)) finds that Li2MnO3 is electrochemically activated above 4.5 V on delithiation, and bulk charge neutrality is mainly maintained by oxidation of a portion of oxygen ions from O²⁻ to O¹⁻. - Operando XAS on Li-rich Li\(_{1.20}\)Mn\(_{0.54}\)Co\(_{0.13}\)Ni\(_{0.13}\)O\(_2\) supports oxygen participation as a reversible redox center, not only as oxygen loss. - Other reports associate the activation/charge compensation with oxide-ion oxidation including O₂ release and peroxo-like O₂²⁻ species. However, O²⁻/O¹⁻ migration barriers remain high, impeding oxygen release from the bulk, while oxygen-vacancy formation becomes thermodynamically favorable for \(x < 1\).  **Consequences and degradation** - The 4.5 V plateau leads to irreversible capacity and is tied to Li2MnO3 activation. - High-voltage oxygen-redox reactions in Li-rich cathodes can drive parasitic reactions such as electrolyte oxidation and O₂ gas evolution. - Irreversible oxygen oxidation can lead to oxygen release and vacancy formation, followed by transition-metal migration, layered-to-spinel/rock-salt reconstruction, activation of lower-voltage redox, surface reconstruction, impedance growth, and voltage decay. Li2MnO3 also undergoes partial layered-to-spinel Li₂Mn₂O₄ transition during initial cycling.  **Kinetics/factors** - The activation plateau above 4.5 V becomes longer for Li2MnO3 samples with lower crystallinity and smaller particle size; lattice defects affecting Li⁺ mobility are suggested as a critical variable in electrochemical activation. - Activating Li2MnO3 at 0 °C can make the >4.5 V plateau stepwise during initial cycling, increasing discharge capacity, improving capacity retention, and stabilizing voltage hysteresis in later cycling.  **Key sources:**   - Li-rich plateau/activation: https://www.fleckmech.org/papers/379.pdf   - Operando XAS/O redox: https://pubs-acs-org-443.webvpna.lzu.edu.cn/doi/full/10.1021/acs.chemmater.3c01446   - Oxygen-redox degradation: https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2950264026000687   - Li2MnO3 activation kinetics: https://library.cnu.ac.kr/eds/detail/edsker_edsker.000005143478   - First-principles Li2MnO3 activation: https://www.osti.gov/biblio/1511383   - Li2MnO3 initial-charge plateau/phase transformation: https://beta.iopscience.iop.org/article/10.1149/MA2017-02/2/129   REMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks.
